<h1>Run Script from File</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Modules &gt; Macros &gt; Run Script from File</b></span><span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>.</b></i></span></p>
<p class="Description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> The <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Run Script from File</b></span> command allows executing a sequence of macro commands on a single or multiple files.</p>
<p>Call <i>Modules &gt; Macros &gt; Run Script from File</i> command. The following dialog will appear:</p>
<p><img src="../Images/Image13.gif" width="377px" height="354px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;">On current document</i></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This option sets the script to be executed for a single or for the current document (it depends on the script content).</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;">On multiple files</i></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This option sets the script to be executed for selected files. Press Choose button to select the files.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><img src="../Images/Image14.gif" width="369px" height="242px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Add File to List</b></span> button allows you to add files that are to be loaded and script executed for them.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Delete Files From List</b></span> allows you to remove files from the execution list.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Choose script</b></span> button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Press this button to browse for a script file. Default extension is .txt.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><i style="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal;">Values for custom parameters</i></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">You can customise some of the parameters of the macro commands in the script. This table is for setting such values for such <a href="../Parameter_Types.htm">customised parameters</a>. The columns are as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Variable</i></span> - name of the custom parameter, e.g. <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%1%</b></span> will be displayed as <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>1</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%Limit edges%</b></span> will be displayed as <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Limit edges</b></span>. This column has read-only fields. The table is sorted alphabetically by Variable column.</p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Value</i></span> - value of the custom parameter. The fields are editable and values for the corresponding variables can be typed or selected. In execution of the script each custom parameter is replaced by its value but the script file is not changed. For enumerated values such as (Yes, No), (On, Off, Toggle), etc. the cell contains a drop-down list with all available values for the particular parameter and the user can select a value instead of typing it.</p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Macros</i></span> - list of macros that contain the custom parameter.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: When a variable is used in more than one macro, the usage of this variable must be conformant with specification of particular parameters in macros usages list, e.g. variable used as numeric (integer or floating point number) parameter in one macro and the same variable used as for example boolean (Yes, No) parameter in other macro. In case with non-compatible variable used, "ERROR" will be displayed in the value cell for that variable</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" id="P1">For example, the following script will generate error:<span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><br>
<br>
SelAll<br>
FillHoles( Method="</span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-weight:bold;"><b>%method%</b></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">", LimitEdges=%Limit edges%, MaxEdges=%Max edges% )<br>
SelAll<br>
Decimate( Accuracy=100, Method="</span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-weight:bold;"><b>%method%</b></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">", MaxDist=%1%, RmBnd=Yes )</span><br>
<br>
<img src="../Images/Image25.gif" width="377px" height="354px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""><br>
<br>
The same variable <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>%method%</b></span> is used for <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Method</i></span> parameter in <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">FillHoles</span> and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Method</i></span> parameter in <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">Decimate</span>. In <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">FillHoles</span> <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Method</i></span> parameter accepts <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>CrvBased</b></span> and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>FlatFIll</b></span> values and in <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">Decimate</span> <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Method</i></span> parameter accepts <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3dDist</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pcent</b></span>, and<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>MaxEdgeLength</b></span> values.</p>
